<title>USA: Hightec acquires Benefits Administration.</title>
<headline>Hightec acquires Benefits Administration.</headline>
<dateline>TIBURON, Calif. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hightec Inc said Friday it has reached final agreements with the shareholders of Benefits Administration Inc to exchange 25 million shares of Hightec for all of the outstanding shares of Benefits Administration, a provider of private label benefit services.</p>
<p>Tom Kidd, president of Benefits, became the majority shareholder, chairman and chief executive officer of Hightec.</p>
<p>Larry Stockett remains president and chief operating officer.</p>
<p>Hightec is a holding company which owns the IPO Network, Benefits, 40 percent of Sinclare Group Inc and Karate International Corp.</p>
</text>
